   "title": "Organization names in seven languages",
   "scope": "Every news agency, observatory, academy, learned society and college named by the record corpus. Names only; what an organization did on a given day belongs to the record, not here.",
   "fields": "key = organization identifier. kind = agency | observatory | academy. latin = the organization's own name in its own language, which is what a reader chasing the source will search for. abbr = the forms a dateline actually prints, which is what ties 「(H. N.)」 in a 1927 Dutch paper to 荷兰新闻社 in the translation. seat / since / until = where and when, given only where the corpus needs them to tell two bodies apart. provenance = the evidence for the expansion, per row, because an expansion without one is an assertion. zh-Hans / zh-Hant / en / fr / es / it / ja = display names, all seven required.",
   "provenance": "Hand-compiled from the names the corpus actually uses. Where an organization's own language is one of the seven, that track carries its own name verbatim (Observatoire de Paris in French, Real Observatorio de Madrid in Spanish, Osservatorio di Brera in Italian). The four Dutch and British agencies keep their own names in the Latin-script tracks because no settled rendering exists in French, Spanish or Italian. French names are capitalised throughout: this is a table of names, not running prose, where French would lower-case a descriptive reference.",
